{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"SEC-CI","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/lib/sandbox-mount.sh","line":513,"code_snippet":"PROJECT_ROOT=\"$ws\" bash \"$ubs\" --opt-out \"eval sandbox: br not on PATH\"","finding":"init_sandbox_beads executes $ws/.claude/scripts/beads/update-beads-state.sh — a copy of the MOUNTED tree's code — on the host, in the driver's environment, whenever br is not on PATH (the documented default: Dockerfile.ablation:82-84). Violates the harness's own trust boundary (sandbox-mount.sh:75, pipeline-run.sh:125-126).","reasoning_trace":"Traced pipeline-run.sh:489 lib_call init_sandbox_beads → sandbox-mount.sh:505 command -v br (absent on this host) → :511-513 bash on the sandbox copy of the mounted tree (mount_prompt_surface :131 copies $SOURCE_TREE/.claude). Base execute-agent.sh has no beads step, so the path is new in this PR.","critique":"The eval.yml trust-boundary scan looks for `source` lines; `bash \"$ubs\"` evades it while doing the same thing.","remediation":"Write the opt-out marker from the harness itself (the script only writes $PROJECT_ROOT/.run/beads-state.json), or run the trusted copy $_SM_REPO_ROOT/.claude/scripts/beads/update-beads-state.sh with PROJECT_ROOT=$ws, or run the step inside the container.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/829.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"CQ-EH","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":702,"code_snippet":"jq -n --arg label \"$label\" …","finding":"`label` is a jq keyword; jq 1.6 (the repository's declared floor, .claude/scripts/lib/dec-write-lib.sh:208) rejects `$label` with 'unexpected label, expecting IDENT'. Same at :816, :881, sandbox-mount.sh:462,467; and the `{name, label, …}` shorthand at ablation-row.sh:285 fails with 'unexpected }'. Every mounted phase dies at the argv capture; write_sandbox_grimoire fails before the first phase.","reasoning_trace":"Reproduced on this host (jq-1.6): `jq -n --arg label x '$label'` and `jq -n '{a:1,label:2} | {a, label}'` both fail to compile.","remediation":"Rename the jq variable (e.g. --arg lbl) at the five sites; write `\"label\": .label` in ablation-row.sh; or declare and check jq >= 1.7 and add a jq 1.6 CI leg.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/474.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-002","category":"code_quality","criterion":"CQ-EH","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":704,"code_snippet":"jq -Rs 'split(\"\\u0000\") | .[:-1]'","finding":"On jq 1.6 the raw slurp of NUL-terminated elements yields no trailing empty element, so `.[:-1]` drops the LAST real element of argv, env and launcher captures: `--effort medium` loses `medium`, `--resume <sid>` loses the id, the env capture loses LOA_ADVERSARIAL_REVIEW_ENFORCE=false. took-effect.sh then reports false FAILs (enforce_env_false, effort_flag_medium, implementer_single_session), and a run whose offending element was last would pass.","reasoning_trace":"Reproduced: printf '%s\\0' a b c | jq -Rs 'split(\"\\u0000\") | .[:-1]' → [\"a\",\"b\"] on jq-1.6.","remediation":"Build the arrays without relying on a trailing separator (`rtrimstr(\"\\u0000\") | split(\"\\u0000\")`, or `--args`/$ARGS.positional); add a test asserting the last argv element and last env key are captured.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/474.html"]}
{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"CQ-EH","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/harness/ablation-row.sh","line":226,"code_snippet":"--argjson minv \"$MINV\" --argjson er \"$ENV_REVIEW\" --argjson ea \"$ENV_AUDIT\"","finding":"The whole MODELINV ledger, the full pipeline.json and both envelopes are passed as --argjson argv strings; Linux caps one argv string at 128 KiB, so a long run's row is never written (set -e aborts before ROW) and runs.jsonl silently lacks the long, expensive runs.","reasoning_trace":"Reproduced: a 140001-byte --argjson → '/usr/bin/jq: Argument list too long'. Confirmed by the review's dissent DISS-001 and the review.","remediation":"Write the inputs to files and use --slurpfile/--rawfile, or stream the ledger on stdin; add a test with a >128 KiB model-invoke.jsonl.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html"]}
{"id":"DO-001","category":"devops","criterion":"DO-DS","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.github/workflows/bats-tests.yml","line":178,"code_snippet":"bash tools/check-manifest-paths.sh\nbash tools/gen-checksums.sh --check","finding":"The new gate compares the committed .claude/checksums.json with the tracked tree, but this PR changes sixteen tracked .claude/ files and does not regenerate the manifest; the gate (and MP-6, tests/unit/check-manifest-paths.bats:88) is red on the PR's own head in every scenario (stale manifest → drift exit 1; absent manifest → exit 1/2).","reasoning_trace":"Diff file list: 16 .claude/ paths changed, .claude/checksums.json absent from the diff. The workspace manifest matches head hashes only because the harness regenerated the sandbox manifest (regen_sandbox_manifest), which says nothing about upstream.","remediation":"Run tools/gen-checksums.sh on the head tree and commit .claude/checksums.json in this PR; make the release path regenerate it.","confidence":"high","references":["https://owasp.org/www-project-top-10-ci-cd-security-risks/CICD-SEC-01-Insufficient-Flow-Control-Mechanisms"]}
