{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"SEC-CI","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/check-loa.sh","line":75,"code_snippet":"elif [[ \"$submodule_mount\" == \"true\" && -f \".loa/${file}\" ]]; then not_mounted=$((not_mounted + 1))","finding":"In a submodule mount every manifest path exists under .loa/<path> by construction, so `Missing:` is unreachable: a deleted or unlinked guard script, hook or gate now prints an informational not-mounted count and 'Integrity verified' where it failed before.","reasoning_trace":"Read of the diff hunk; confirmed by cross-model DISS-C-001 and the review.","remediation":"Classify not-mounted only for paths outside the link scope mount-submodule.sh creates; fail for an absent path inside it (at minimum for .claude/scripts and .claude/hooks).","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/354.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"SEC-CI","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/lib/sandbox-mount.sh","line":386,"code_snippet":"\"$tool\" --root \"$ws\" >/dev/null 2>&1","finding":"regen_sandbox_manifest executes ${EVAL_PROMPT_TREE}/tools/gen-checksums.sh — the tree under test — which `source`s that tree's .claude/scripts/compat-lib.sh (gen-checksums.sh:51), contradicting the header's 'never .claude/ code'. Unreachable from pipeline-run.sh today (:476 excludes /.claude/ from the sandbox repo), so dead code carrying a trust hole.","reasoning_trace":"Branch condition :384-385 requires git ls-files .claude non-empty; pipeline-run.sh excludes .claude; execute-agent.sh never git-inits the workspace.","remediation":"Delete the tool branch; keep the inline hashlib path, or run only the trusted copy under $_SM_REPO_ROOT.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/829.html"]}
{"id":"DO-003","category":"devops","criterion":"DO-DS","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/Dockerfile.ablation","line":19,"code_snippet":"FROM rust:1-bookworm AS brbuild\nRUN cargo install beads_rust --version 0.2.6 …","finding":"The brbuild stage is never COPY --from'd and :82 says the crate is not on crates.io; under the classic builder (DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0) every stage is built and the image build fails.","reasoning_trace":"No COPY --from=brbuild anywhere in the Dockerfile; the comment at :82-84 records the decision not to ship br.","remediation":"Delete the stage.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1164.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"SEC-AZ","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/evals/harness/pipeline-run.sh","line":570,"code_snippet":"if [[ -f \"$CREDS_HOME/.codex/$f\" ]]; then cp \"$CREDS_HOME/.codex/$f\" \"$HOME_DIR/.codex/$f\"; fi","finding":"The operator's codex auth.json is copied into the per-run HOME that is bind-mounted rw into the container for EVERY container arm, including arms that never run a codex hop (a0_bare, a4_no_gates); the agent under test reads it with --network bridge. remove_tree runs only on trapped exits, so a SIGKILLed driver leaves the copy under meta/home.","reasoning_trace":"make_home :563-573 runs unconditionally in container mode (:574); GATES_OFF/LOA_MOUNT are known at :419-421 before it.","remediation":"Copy the codex files only when the arm's phase set includes a gate and gates are on; fail closed if meta/home exists at start; document the residual-on-SIGKILL case.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html"]}
